          "code": "DISPLAY_MONITORING_PROMPT_TEMPLATES",
          "id": "1776347678974",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776347678975_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_MONITORING_PROMPT_TEMPLATES_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for monitoring prompt template records. You must adhere to the standard `oraInfoDisplay` Knowledge Base.\n\nYour task is to produce exactly 2 top-level blocks in this exact order:\n\n1. one `oraInfoDisplay` block  \n2. one `oraInsight` block for Create  \n\nDo not output anything else.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES**\n\n- Do not output markdown\n- Do not output explanation\n- Do not output prose\n- Do not output code fences\n- Do not output plain JSON objects by themselves\n- Every action must be wrapped in `<oraInsight>...</oraInsight>`\n- Do not use `<actionableInsight>`\n- Do not omit the `<oraInsight>` tags\n- Do not place actions inside `oraInfoDisplay`\n- Do not place actions in an array\n- Do not place actions in an `\"actions\"` property\n\n**INPUT**\n\n- Monitoring prompt template data: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_MONITORING_PROMPT_TEMPLATES_DATA.$output.result}}\n\n**INPUT RULES**\n\n- The input is a real JSON object containing an `items` array\n- Read values from the input object\n- Preserve full row objects exactly when passing `rowData`\n- Never output literal field-path names such as:\n  - `monitoringPrompt`\n  - `categoryCodeMeaning`\n  - `frequencyCodeMeaning`\n- Use actual values from input\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION**\n\n- The root `oraInfoDisplay` must include:\n - `title`: `New monitoring prompt`\n - `description`: `Select a sample monitoring prompt from the options in the catalog below and modify it as needed. To create your own prompt, skip the catalog selection, and continue.`\n\n**STRUCTURE RULES**\n\n- Generate exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` using `multiRecordWidget`\n- Treat the input as a JSON object containing an `items` array\n- Use the following columns in this exact order:\n  1. Monitoring Prompt  \n  2. Category  \n  3. Frequency  \n\n**ROW MAPPING RULES**\n\n- Each object in `items` must map to exactly one row\n- Preserve row order exactly as received\n- Do not skip or merge rows\n\nColumn mappings:\n\n- Monitoring Prompt → `monitoringPrompt`\n- Category → `categoryCodeMeaning`\n- Frequency → `frequencyCodeMeaning`\n\n- The `Monitoring Prompt` column must always display the plain text value of `ruleName`\n- Do not remove or replace visible text when applying actions\n\n**DERIVED VALUE RULES**\n\nCategory:\n- Use `categoryCodeMeaning` directly if present\n- If missing or null, omit the value\n\nFrequency:\n- Use `frequencyCodeMeaning` directly if present\n- If missing or null, omit the value\n\n**ROW ACTION AND HYPERLINK RULES**\n- The `Monitoring Prompt` cell must trigger:  \n  `ora.Invoke(\"selectPromptTemplate\", {\"rowData\": <full current row object>, \"actionCode\": \"selectPromptTemplate\"})`\n\nRules:\n- Always display `ruleName` as visible text\n- Pass full row object exactly as received\n- Do not modify, flatten, or remove fields in `rowData`\n- Apply action only to `Monitoring Prompt` column\n\nHyperlink behavior:\n- If supported, render `Monitoring Prompt` as clickable text\n- If hyperlink removes or hides text, revert to plain text\n\nFallback:\n- If cell-level hyperlink is unsupported:\n  - Add a separate action column  \n  - That column must invoke the same `ora.Invoke(...)`\n- Only add fallback column when required\n\n**TOP-LEVEL ACTION BLOCK**\n\nAfter the closing `oraInfoDisplay`, output exactly 1 `<oraInsight>` block for Create.\n\nThe `<oraInsight>` block must follow this shape:\n\n{  \n  \"title\": \"Skip and continue\",  \n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",  \n  \"actionText\": \"Skip and continue\",  \n  \"followUpCommand\": `ora.Invoke(\"selectPromptTemplate\", {\"actionCode\": \"selectPromptTemplate\", \"rowData\": {} })`  \n}\n\n**CONSTRAINTS**\n\n- Do not add checkbox column\n- Do not add extra columns unless fallback is required\n- Do not summarize data\n- Do not invent values\n- Omit missing/null mapped values unless explicitly defined\n- Use only `multiRecordWidget`\n\n**OUTPUT RULES**\n\n- Output only the final `oraInfoDisplay` followed by exactly one `<oraInsight>` block\n- No markdown\n- No explanations\n- No extra text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Process Selected Monitoring Prompt Template",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawInput = $context.$app.$OraAction || $context.$system.$inputMessage;\n\nlet rowData = {};\n\nfunction normalizeKey(key) {\n  return String(key)\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \"\");\n}\n\nfunction normalizeObjectKeys(obj) {\n  return Object.entries(obj || {}).reduce((acc, [key, value]) => {\n    acc[normalizeKey(key)] = value;\n    return acc;\n  }, {});\n}\n\ntry {\n  const inputMessage = rawInput || \"\";\n\n  if (inputMessage) {\n    let parsedInput = JSON.parse(inputMessage);\n\n    // handle double-encoded JSON\n    if (typeof parsedInput === \"string\") {\n      parsedInput = JSON.parse(parsedInput);\n    }\n\n    rowData = normalizeObjectKeys(parsedInput?.rowData || {});\n  }\n} catch (e) {}\n\nreturn rowData;"
          },
