          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780936626751_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PROMPT_POLICY_STATUS.$output}}.\nCurrentStatus: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_PROMPT_STATUS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.status}}\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Oracle Response payloads.\n\n**Directive:**\n\n1. Your sole purpose is to use a valid `oraInfoDisplay` output using the empty `messageListWidget`.\n\n**Root configuration:**\n\nDetermine the root `title` from `ChangeStatus` only:\n\n1. If `ChangeStatus` is `Enabled`, set the root `title`\n   exactly to:\n   Monitoring Prompt has been Disabled successfully.\n\n2. If `ChangeStatus` is `Disabled`, set the root `title`\n   exactly to:\n   Monitoring Prompt has been Enabled successfully.\n\n**Output requirement:**\n- Only show `Title` (from `Root configuration`) in `oraInfoDisplay`.\n- Do not include markdown, explanations, comments, or extra text.\n- Do not invent, remove, or modify any payload fields.\n- Do not answer unrelated substance.\n- For personal questions, respond only with a brief capability statement tied to Oracle AI Studio UI/action prompt generation.\n- For self-harm, violence, abuse, or immediate-safety topics, follow platform safety rules first."
            }
          ],
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1780994476855",
          "code": "PROCESS_SELECTED_PROMPT_TO_DUPLICATE",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Process Selected Prompt to Duplicate",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawInput = $context.$app.$OraAction || $context.$system.$inputMessage;\n\nlet rowData = {};\n\nfunction normalizeKey(key) {\n  return String(key)\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \"\");\n}\n\nfunction normalizeObjectKeys(obj) {\n  return Object.entries(obj || {}).reduce((acc, [key, value]) => {\n    acc[normalizeKey(key)] = value;\n    return acc;\n  }, {});\n}\n\ntry {\n  const inputMessage = rawInput || \"\";\n\n  if (inputMessage) {\n    let parsedInput = JSON.parse(inputMessage);\n\n    // handle double-encoded JSON\n    if (typeof parsedInput === \"string\") {\n      parsedInput = JSON.parse(parsedInput);\n    }\n\n    rowData = normalizeObjectKeys(parsedInput?.rowData || {});\n  }\n} catch (e) {}\n\nreturn rowData;"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11490,
            "y": 7870
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780994476856"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1780994476856",
          "code": "DISPLAY_SELECTED_PROMPT_TEMPLATE_FOR_DUPLICATE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Selected Prompt Template for Duplicate",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11445,
            "y": 8092
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776406680162_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input - {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_SELECTED_PROMPT_TO_DUPLICATE.$output.result}}\nAdmin - {{$context.$variables.isAdmin}}\n\nOptions:\n- FrequencyOptions = {{$context.$variables.OraFunRuleFrequency}} or []\n- PriorityOptions = {{$context.$variables.OraFUNRulePriority}} or []\n- CategoryOptions = {{$context.$variables.OraGLRuleCategory}} or []\n\nRules for options:\n\n- Always use the above resolved options variables\n- Never omit \"options\" for select fields\n- If any options variable is missing or null, use []\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Monitoring Prompt Create Form.\n\nYour task is to produce exactly 1 top-level block.\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\n\nCritical rules:\n\n- Do not output markdown\n- Do not output explanation\n- Do not output prose\n- Do not output code fences\n- Do not output plain JSON objects by themselves\n- Do not output any additional blocks\n- Do not output any actions\n- Do not place actions in an array\n- Do not place actions in an \"actions\" property\n\nInput rules:\n\n- The input is a real JSON object with real values\n- Read values from the input object\n- Never output literal field-path names such as:\n  - \"monitoringPrompt\"\n  - \"categoryCode\"\n  - \"frequencyCode\"\n  - \"rulePriorityCode\"\n- Use actual values from input\n\nCreate form block rules:\n\n- Output exactly one block\n- Inside include exactly one JSON object\n- Use this exact shape:\n\n{\n  \"patternId\": \"recordWidget\",\n  \"title\": \"Duplicate\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": \"monitoringPromptCreateForm\",\n    \"readOnly\": false,\n    \"submitText\": \"Save\",\n    \"fields\": [ ... ]\n  }\n}\n\nField rendering rules:\n\n- Always render all 5 mandatory fields: Monitoring Prompt, Frequency, Time Frame, Priority, Category\n- If `Admin` is `true`: render additional 2 fields: Recipient Type, Recipients\n- Never omit a field, even if its value is missing\n- If a mapped value is missing, use an empty string as the field value\n- Keep the fields in this exact order:\n  1. Monitoring Prompt\n  2. Frequency\n  3. Time Frame\n  4. Priority\n  5. Category\n  6. Recipient Type (Only if `Admin` is `true`)\n  7. Recipients (Only if `Admin` is `true`)\n\nField definitions:\n\n1. Monitoring Prompt\n- \"id\": \"monitoringPrompt\"\n- \"type\": \"textarea\"\n- \"label\": \"Monitoring Prompt\"\n- default value = mapped value from monitoringprompt, or \"\"\n\n2. Frequency\n- \"id\": \"frequency\"\n- \"type\": \"select\"\n- \"label\": \"Frequency\"\n- \"required\": true\n- default value = mapped value from frequencycode, or \"\"\n- options: FrequencyOptions\n\n3. Time Frame\n- \"id\": \"timeFrame\"\n- \"type\": \"text\"\n- \"label\": \"Time Frame\"\n- default value = mapped value from timeframe or \"\"\n\n4. Priority\n- \"id\": \"priority\"\n- \"type\": \"select\"\n- \"label\": \"Priority\"\n- \"required\": true\n- default value = mapped value from ruleprioritycode, or \"\"\n- options: PriorityOptions\n\n5. Category\n- \"id\": \"category\"\n- \"type\": \"select\"\n- \"label\": \"Category\"\n- \"required\": true\n- default value = mapped value from categorycode, or \"\"\n- options: CategoryOptions\n\n6. Recipient Type\n- \"id\": \"recipientType\"\n- \"type\": \"select\"\n- \"label\": \"Recipient Type\"\n- default value = \"User\"\n- options: [\"User\",\"Role\"]\n\n7. Recipients\n- \"id\": \"recipients\"\n- \"type\": \"textArea\"\n- \"label\": \"Recipients\"\n- default value = \"\"\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Do not mark the form as readonly\n- Do not add submit\n- Do not add readOnlyFields\n- Do not add actions\n- Do not add title text beyond specified\n- Do not add description text beyond specified\n- Do not omit any of the 5 fields\n- Do not hide any field based on missing values\n- Use only actual input-derived defaults\n- If a mapped value is missing, use empty string for the field value\n\nFinal Output Format:\n\n{\n  \"patternId\": \"recordWidget\",\n  \"title\": \"Duplicate\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": \"monitoringPromptCreateForm\",\n    \"readOnly\": false,\n    \"submitText\": \"Save\",\n    \"fields\": [ ... ]\n  }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "enableActions": true,
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_RECORD"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1780713359692",
          "code": "GENERATE_SUBTITLE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Subtitle",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 13677,
            "y": 7426
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780713359692_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Ledger Operations text rendering assistant.\n\nUse only these inputs:\nledgerName = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.ledgerName}}\nperiodName = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.periodName}}\nendDate = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.endDate}}\ncurrentDate = {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nCalculate `daysDifference` as the integer day difference:\n`endDate - currentDate`\n\nFormat the status text as follows:\n\n- If `$daysDifference = 1`, return `Day - 1`\n- If `$daysDifference > 1`, return `Day - {daysDifference}`\n- If `$daysDifference = 0`, return `Day - 0`\n- If `$daysDifference = -1`, return `1 day after close`\n- If `$daysDifference < -1`, return `{absolute value of daysDifference} days after close`\n\nReturn only one plain-text line in this exact order:\n{ledgerName}    {periodName}    {daysToClose}\n\nSpacing rule:\n- Between values, use exactly four literal Unicode non-breaking space\n  characters: U+00A0 U+00A0 U+00A0 U+00A0.\n- Do not use normal spaces for the separators."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1781000039004",
          "code": "EXTRACT_QUERY_INTENT",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Query Intent",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 12147,
            "y": 7426
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781000039005"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780655628823_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "input_message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nYou are an intent classifier and filter extractor for searching monitoring prompts.\n\nClassify the input_message for monitoring-prompt search requests.\n\nAllowed category:\n- searchMonitoringPrompts\n\nFor this classifier, the words \"prompt\" and \"prompts\" refer to monitoring prompts unless the user clearly means something else.\n\nReturn searchMonitoringPrompts when the user explicitly asks to search, show, display, get, find, list, or filter prompts or monitoring prompts using at least one searchable filter.\n\nIf the user is not asking to retrieve matching prompts or monitoring prompts using at least one searchable filter, still output searchMonitoringPrompts with all filter arrays empty.\n\nSearchable filters:\n- frequency\n- category\n- priority\n- status\n- ruleName\n\nSupported frequency values:\n- Hourly\n- Daily\n- Weekly\n- Monthly\n- Quarterly\n- Yearly\n\nFrequency normalization:\n- Map minor spelling, pluralization, or wording deviations to the closest supported frequency value.\n- Map hour, hourly, every hour to Hourly.\n- Map day, daily, every day to Daily.\n- Map week, weekly, every week to Weekly.\n- Map month, monthly, every month to Monthly.\n- Map quarter, quarterly, every quarter to Quarterly.\n- Map year, yearly, annually, annual, every year to Yearly.\n- Do not invent a frequency when the user does not mention one.\n\nSupported priority values:\n- High\n- Medium\n- Low\n\nPriority extraction:\n- Extract priority only when the user explicitly mentions one of the supported priorities.\n- Preserve the priority text as entered by the user.\n- Do not treat priority words as category.\n\nSupported status values:\n- Enabled\n- Disabled\n\nStatus normalization:\n- Map supported synonyms and close variants to the supported status value.\n- Map enabled, enable, active, activated, on, turned on, and running to Enabled.\n- Map disabled, disable, inactive, deactivated, off, turned off, stopped, and paused to Disabled.\n- Do not invent a status when the user does not mention one.\n\nFrequency extraction:\n- Extract frequency only when the user explicitly mentions a supported frequency value, synonym, or close variant.\n- Normalize the extracted value to exactly one of:\n  Hourly, Daily, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly, Yearly.\n- If multiple frequencies are present, include all normalized values.\n- Do not treat frequency words as category.\n\nStatus extraction:\n- Extract status only when the user explicitly mentions enabled, disabled, or a supported synonym.\n- Normalize the extracted value to exactly one of:\n  Enabled, Disabled.\n- If multiple statuses are present, include all normalized values.\n- Do not treat status words as category.\n\nCategory extraction:\n- Categories are free-form.\n- The category does not need to match any predefined list.\n- Extract category values directly from the user input when they are used as filters for prompts or monitoring prompts.\n- Extract category when the user provides a category-like word or phrase before \"prompt\", \"prompts\", \"monitoring prompt\", or \"monitoring prompts\".\n- For phrases like \"enabled variance prompts\", extract Enabled as status and variance as category.\n- Preserve the category text as entered by the user.\n- Category values may be single words or multi-word phrases.\n- Do not invent category values.\n- Do not treat frequency, status, priority, or rule name values as category.\n- Do not treat search verbs as category.\n- Do not treat the words \"monitoring\", \"prompt\", or \"prompts\" as category.\n\nRule name extraction:\n- Extract ruleName when the user mentions \"rule\", \"rule name\", \"named\", or provides a quoted rule-like phrase.\n- Preserve the ruleName text as entered by the user, except remove surrounding quotes.\n- Do not treat category, frequency, status, or priority words as ruleName.\n\nDo not infer filter values from vague mentions of prompts or monitoring prompts.\nDo not invent filter values.\nExtract only values directly present or clearly implied by the user input.\n\nOutput rules:\n\nOutput only valid JSON:\n\n{\n  \"code\": \"searchMonitoringPrompts\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"frequency\": [],\n    \"category\": [],\n    \"priority\": [],\n    \"status\": [],\n    \"ruleName\": []\n  }\n}\n\nRules:\n- code must be exactly: searchMonitoringPrompts\n- always include filters\n- filters.frequency must contain only extracted and normalized frequency values\n- filters.category must contain only category values extracted from the user input\n- filters.priority must contain only extracted priority values\n- filters.status must contain only extracted and normalized status values\n- filters.ruleName must contain only extracted rule names\n- if multiple values are present for one filter, include all values\n- do not include explanations, markdown, or extra text\n- do not include any root-level key other than code and filters\n- do not output value\n- do not output values\n- do not output filter\n- do not output arrays outside the filters object\n\nOut-of-scope and safety behavior:\n- Do not answer unrelated questions or personal questions.\n- For unrelated or personal questions, return the valid JSON object with code searchMonitoringPrompts and empty filter arrays.\n- For self-harm, violence, abuse, or immediate-safety topics, follow platform safety rules first. Do not provide instructions, operational details, or detailed counseling."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1781000039005",
          "code": "PREPARE_PAYLOAD_FOR_QUERY",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Payload For Query",
            "sourceCode": "const normalizeText = (value) => {\n  return String(value ?? \"\")\n    .trim()\n    .toLowerCase();\n};\n\nconst buildOrLikeFilter = (field, values = [], shouldNormalize = true) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(values) || !values.length) return \"\";\n\n  const validValues = values\n    .map(value =>\n      shouldNormalize\n        ? normalizeText(value)\n        : String(value ?? \"\").trim()\n    )\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  if (!validValues.length) return \"\";\n\n  return `(${validValues\n    .map(value => `${field} ~like '%${value}%'`)\n    .join(\" OR \")})`;\n};\n\nconst buildCategoryCodeLookupMap = () => {\n  const categoryCodeLookup = $context.$variables.OraGLRuleCategory ?? [];\n\n  const categoryMap = new Map();\n\n  categoryCodeLookup.forEach((item) => {\n    const code = item?.LookupCode;\n    const label = item?.Meaning;\n\n    if (!code) return;\n\n    if (label) {\n      categoryMap.set(normalizeText(label), code);\n    }\n\n    categoryMap.set(normalizeText(code), code);\n  });\n\n  return categoryMap;\n};\n\nconst mapCategoriesToCodes = (categories = []) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(categories) || !categories.length) return [];\n\n  const categoryMap = buildCategoryCodeLookupMap();\n\n  return categories\n    .map(category => categoryMap.get(normalizeText(category)))\n    .filter(Boolean);\n};\n\nconst buildLedgerInsightsQuery = ({\n  status = [],\n  frequency = [],\n  categories = [],\n  priority = [],\n  ruleNames = []\n} = {}) => {\n  const mappedCategoryCodes = mapCategoriesToCodes(categories);\n\n  const categoryFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"categoryCode\",\n    mappedCategoryCodes,\n    false\n  );\n\n  const freqFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"schedule.frequency.meaning\",\n    frequency\n  );\n\n  const priorityFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"rulePriority.meaning\",\n    priority\n  );\n\n  const ruleNameFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"ruleName\",\n    ruleNames\n  );\n\n  const filters = [\n    categoryFilter,\n    freqFilter,\n    priorityFilter,\n    ruleNameFilter\n  ].filter(Boolean);\n\n  let statusParam;\n\n  if (status.length === 1) {\n    statusParam = `policyEnabled=${status[0] === \"Enabled\"}`;\n  } else {\n    statusParam = \"policyEnabled=true\";\n  }\n\n  return [\n    statusParam,\n    filters.length ? `$filter=${filters.join(\" AND \")}` : \"\",\n    `$sortBy=rulePriority.displaySequence:asc,timeCreated:desc`,\n    `sensorCode=LedgerInsights`,\n    `catalog=false`\n  ].filter(Boolean).join(\"&\");\n};\n\nconst intent = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_QUERY_INTENT?.$output;\n\nconst searchFilters = intent?.filters ?? {};\n\nlet statusFilter = searchFilters.status ?? [];\nlet frequencyFilter = searchFilters.frequency ?? [];\nlet categoryFilter = searchFilters.category ?? [];\nlet priorityFilter = searchFilters.priority ?? [];\nlet ruleNameFilter = searchFilters.ruleName ?? [];\n\nconst mappedCategoryCodes = mapCategoriesToCodes(categoryFilter);\n\nconst hasNoFilters =\n  statusFilter.length === 0 &&\n  frequencyFilter.length === 0 &&\n  categoryFilter.length === 0 &&\n  priorityFilter.length === 0 &&\n  ruleNameFilter.length === 0;\n\nconst hasOnlyUnmappedCategoryIntent =\n  statusFilter.length === 0 &&\n  frequencyFilter.length === 0 &&\n  categoryFilter.length > 0 &&\n  mappedCategoryCodes.length === 0 &&\n  priorityFilter.length === 0 &&\n  ruleNameFilter.length === 0;\n\nif (hasNoFilters || hasOnlyUnmappedCategoryIntent) {\n  const enteredQuery = String($context.$system.$inputMessage ?? \"\").trim();\n\n  if (enteredQuery) {\n    ruleNameFilter.push(enteredQuery);\n  }\n}\n\nif (statusFilter.length === 0) {\n  statusFilter.push(\"Enabled\");\n}\n\nconst query = buildLedgerInsightsQuery({\n  status: statusFilter,\n  frequency: frequencyFilter,\n  categories: categoryFilter,\n  priority: priorityFilter,\n  ruleNames: ruleNameFilter\n});\n\nreturn {\n  query,\n  status: statusFilter[0]\n};",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 12147,
            "y": 7648
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781000039006"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1781000039006",
          "code": "FETCH_MONITORING_PROMPTS_FOR_USER_QUERY",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fetch Monitoring Prompts For User Query",
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_FIN_GENERALLED_SENSORPOLICIES",
            "functionName": "get_sensorPolicyList"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 12091.5,
            "y": 7870
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781000039007"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781000039006_qParam",
              "name": "qParam",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_PAYLOAD_FOR_QUERY.$output.result.query}}",
              "required": true,
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1781000039007",
          "code": "PROCESS_MONITORING_PROMPTS_QUERY_DATA",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Process Monitoring Prompts Query Data",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let input = $context.$nodes.FETCH_MONITORING_PROMPTS_FOR_USER_QUERY.$output;\nlet totalLen = input?.items?.length || 0;\n\n// return { items : [], itemsLen : 0, totalLen : 0 };\n\nlet categoryCodeLookup = $context.$variables.OraGLRuleCategory ?? [];\n\nlet recipientType = undefined;\n\nfunction getAssignedUsers(data) {\n  const assignedUsers = data\n    .filter(item => item.actionParameters)\n    .flatMap(item => {\n      const parsed = JSON.parse(atob(item.actionParameters));\n\n      const recipients = parsed?.recipients || [];\n      const type = recipients.find(r => r.type)?.type;\n\n      if (type === \"ORA_USER\") {\n        recipientType = \"User\";\n      } else if (type === \"ORA_ROLE\") {\n        recipientType = \"Role\";\n      } else {\n        recipientType = undefined;\n      }\n\n      return recipients.map(r => r.value);\n    })\n    .filter(Boolean)\n    .join(\",\");\n\n  return assignedUsers;\n}\n\nconst safeDisplayTimeframe = (timespan) => {\n  if (!timespan) {\n    return \"\";\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const parsedTimespan = typeof timespan === \"string\" ? JSON.parse(timespan) : timespan;\n    return parsedTimespan?.displayValue || \"\";\n  } catch (e) {\n    return \"\";\n  }\n};\n\nconst categoryLookup = new Map(\n  categoryCodeLookup.map(item => [item.LookupCode, item])\n);\n\nlet items = (input?.items ?? []).map((row) => ({\n  monitoringPrompt: row?.ruleName,\n\n  categoryCode: row?.categoryCode,\n  categoryCodeMeaning: categoryLookup\n    .get(row?.categoryCode)\n    ?.Meaning,\n\n  frequencyCode: row?.schedule?.frequency?.lookupCode,\n  frequencyCodeMeaning: row?.schedule?.frequency?.meaning,\n\n  timeframe: safeDisplayTimeframe(row?.timespan),\n\n  rulePriorityCode: row?.rulePriority?.lookupCode,\n  rulePriorityCodeMeaning: row?.rulePriority?.meaning,\n\n  createdBy: row?.createdBy?.includes(\"SEED_DATA\") ? \"Oracle\" : row?.createdBy,\n  assignedTo: getAssignedUsers(row.actions.items),\n  recipientType: recipientType,\n  ruleActionTypeCode: row?.ruleActionTypeCode,\n  ruleDescription: row?.ruleDescription,\n  ruleId: row?.ruleId,\n  timeCreated: row?.timeCreated,\n  status: $context.$nodes.PREPARE_PAYLOAD_FOR_QUERY.$output.result.status\n}));\n\nlet returnLimit = -1;\nlet showAll = true;\nreturn {\n  items,\n  itemsLen : items.length,\n  totalLen,\n  hasMore: !showAll && totalLen > items.length\n};"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 12100.5,
            "y": 8092
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781000039008"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
